<title>USA: U.S. proposes to limit shark fishing.</title>
<headline>U.S. proposes to limit shark fishing.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Marine Fisheries Service Thursday proposed cutting recreational and commercial fishing of coastal sharks to help stem the decline of five Atlantic species.</p>
<p>The proposal would issue permits based on catches of sharks in 1994 and 1995, reducing commercial quotas for large coastal sharks and establishing a quota for small coastal sharks for the first time.</p>
<p>It would bar fishermen from retaining basking, sand tiger, bigeye sand tiger, white, and whale sharks and limit fishing of white sharks to recreational catch and releases.</p>
</text>
